        "original_id": "4c5d2390-5303-5ec9-9a68-280898289314",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Kristensen, Petter Solberg, David Coulthard, Pascal Wehrlein, Hamble James Leacock\n- Events: 2014 Race of Champions, Nations' Cup, individual contest, 24 Hours of Le Mans\n- Places: Bushy Park, Barbados\n- Topics: motorsport records, birth background\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Kristensen holds the record for the most wins at the 24 Hours of Le Mans with nine victories, including six consecutive wins from 2000 to 2005.\n- Bushy Park in Barbados hosted the 2014 Race of Champions later that same year.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, the Nordic team of Tom Kristensen and Petter Solberg won the Nations' Cup.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, David Coulthard won the individual contest by defeating Pascal Wehrlein 2–0 in the final.\n- Hamble James Leacock was born in Barbados, where his father was a slaveholder.",
